      "effective_style_prefix_sha256": "3a680861e4d9d1bc46ddba4dc1fc91f26c68f9f9c5e5e450a85fcba7fda43c2d",
      "fallback_used": false,
      "fallback_attempts": [],
      "attempt_count": 1,
      "asr_text": "At midnight, for seven nights, I slowly opened his door. You should have seen my patience. He never even moved. Then I let one thin ray escape from my lantern, but I always found that eye shut. I could not act. I hated his eye, not him. Every morning, I kindly asked about his night's sleep. On night eight, I almost laughed at my own cleverness. Then my thumb slipped on the catch of my lantern.",
